  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Neuroblast proliferation refers to the growth and division of neuroblasts, which are progenitor cells that develop into neurons during nervous system development."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7832e6342cbbf4e201eb3abbeccf544b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MULTICELLULAR ORGANISM DEVELOPMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Multicellular organism development refers to the processes that lead to the growth and differentiation of a single-celled zygote into a complex multicellular organism."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e66c01e579691c0f359d019a8fc855d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERIPHERAL NERVOUS SYSTEM DEVELOPMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Peripheral nervous system development is influenced by ARTN."&lt;SEP&gt;"Peripheral nervous system development is the process by which the peripheral nerves and ganglia form and mature during embryonic development."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cbf63ccc603ad3e1e231621abcfba496&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7832e6342cbbf4e201eb3abbeccf544b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SPERMATOGENESIS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Spermatogenesis is the process by which male gametes (sperm) are produced from spermatogonial stem cells."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e66c01e579691c0f359d019a8fc855d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SIGNAL TRANSDUCTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Signal transduction refers to the processes by which cells respond to external signals, often through a series of molecular interactions that lead to specific cellular responses."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7832e6342cbbf4e201eb3abbeccf544b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DNA_REPLICATION-DEPENDENT NUCLEOSOME ASSEMBLY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This process involves the assembly of nucleosomes during DNA replication."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e66c01e579691c0f359d019a8fc855d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NEURON_PROJECTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A part of a neuron that extends out to connect with other neurons or cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Neuron projections include axons and dendrites, which extend from the neuron body to facilitate communication with other neurons or cells."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6af7852122b20fd32632d05ee60db0b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3506d0e7e897cc0dd02aaad510a5bdca</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXTRACELLULAR SPACE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The extracellular space is the fluid-filled area outside of cells where various signaling molecules and other substances are exchanged between cells."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7832e6342cbbf4e201eb3abbeccf544b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DNA_REPLICATION-INDEPENDENT NUCLEOSOME ASSEMBLY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This process refers to the assembly of nucleosomes that occurs independently of DNA replication."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e66c01e579691c0f359d019a8fc855d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXTRACELLULAR REGION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The extracellular region is the space outside of cells where various biological processes occur, such as signaling and nutrient exchange."&lt;SEP&gt;"The extracellular region refers to the physical space outside of cells, including tissues and fluids, where cellular interactions occur."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e66c01e579691c0f359d019a8fc855d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7832e6342cbbf4e201eb3abbeccf544b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHROMATIN ASSEMBLY OR DISASSEMBLY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Chromatin assembly and disassembly refer to the dynamic processes of building and breaking down chromatin structures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e66c01e579691c0f359d019a8fc855d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEMBRANE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A general term for biological membranes that separate cellular compartments or enclose cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"A lipid bilayer structure that forms the boundary of cellular compartments or organelles."&lt;SEP&gt;"Membrane is a cellular component where ATAD3A and other proteins are located or part of."&lt;SEP&gt;"Membrane refers to cellular membranes, including nuclear and cytoplasmic membranes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Membranes are lipid bilayers that enclose cells or organelles, regulating the passage of substances in and out."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Membrane is a general term for lipid bilayers that form the boundaries of cellular compartments, with ATG9A and ATG9B being integral components of various membranes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-daff5f83917cc6f9ded289c270e2129b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6af7852122b20fd32632d05ee60db0b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-253eb098498cf4c2d668ce32dfcd8748&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbbe6b035d10996de43125a54fa4ac7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e66c01e579691c0f359d019a8fc855d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1ed23d3600b0b8091acfc263f6b6e3f</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GOLGI APPARATUS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A cellular organelle involved in protein modification, sorting, and transport."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Golgi apparatus is a cellular organelle involved in modifying proteins and dispatching them to their final destinations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Golgi apparatus is a cellular organelle involved in modifying, sorting, and transporting proteins and lipids within the cell."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Golgi apparatus is an organelle involved in modifying, sorting, and packaging proteins for cell secretion or use within the cell."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Golgi apparatus is an organelle involved in the modification, sorting, and packaging of proteins and lipids for transport within the cell or to its exterior."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cbf63ccc603ad3e1e231621abcfba496&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73933ba64ffac4e6b0a92e59eac8d328&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e66c01e579691c0f359d019a8fc855d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1ed23d3600b0b8091acfc263f6b6e3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7832e6342cbbf4e201eb3abbeccf544b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BICELLULAR TIGHT JUNCTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A bicellular tight junction is a type of cell junction that seals off spaces between cells in tissues, preventing the passage of molecules through intercellular spaces."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e66c01e579691c0f359d019a8fc855d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GROWTH_CONE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A growth cone is a structure at the tip of developing axons that plays a role in guiding neuronal connections during development."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3506d0e7e897cc0dd02aaad510a5bdca</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CORTICAL ENDOPLASMIC RETICULUM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A specialized region of the endoplasmic reticulum associated with muscle cells, where ASPH is located."&lt;SEP&gt;"The cortical endoplasmic reticulum refers to regions of the endoplasmic reticulum located near the cell membrane, playing a role in protein synthesis and calcium storage."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d2e53da26ea23302e454287f8e030712&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7832e6342cbbf4e201eb3abbeccf544b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTEGRAL COMPONENT OF PLASMA MEMBRANE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to proteins that are embedded within the plasma membrane, playing roles in cell signaling, transport, and other cellular functions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e66c01e579691c0f359d019a8fc855d</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DENDRITE_MEMBRANE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The membrane covering the dendrites of neurons, involved in receiving signals from other neurons."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6af7852122b20fd32632d05ee60db0b3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENDOPLASMIC RETICULUM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An intracellular organelle responsible for protein synthesis, folding, and lipid metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"The endoplasmic reticulum is a cellular organelle involved in protein synthesis and modification, with ASPH, ASPHD2, and ASPSCR1 being located or active within it."&lt;SEP&gt;"The endoplasmic reticulum is a cellular organelle involved in protein synthesis, lipid metabolism, and calcium storage."&lt;SEP&gt;"The endoplasmic reticulum is a cellular organelle responsible for protein synthesis, lipid metabolism, and calcium storage."&lt;SEP&gt;"The endoplasmic reticulum is involved in protein synthesis, folding, and lipid metabolism, with specific locations like the rough ER mentioned."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-cbf63ccc603ad3e1e231621abcfba496&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73933ba64ffac4e6b0a92e59eac8d328&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2e53da26ea23302e454287f8e030712&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1ed23d3600b0b8091acfc263f6b6e3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7832e6342cbbf4e201eb3abbeccf544b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROTEIN_PHOSPHATASE_2A_BINDING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Protein phosphatase 2A binding involves interactions between proteins and this specific type of phosphatase, which plays a role in dephosphorylating target proteins."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3506d0e7e897cc0dd02aaad510a5bdca</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ECTODERM DIFFERENTIATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ectoderm differentiation is the process by which cells from the ectoderm layer of an embryo develop into specific cell types, such as neurons or skin cells."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7832e6342cbbf4e201eb3abbeccf544b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CYTOPLASMIC_ACTIVITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cytoplasmic activity refers to biochemical processes occurring within the cytoplasm, such as enzyme function or molecular interactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3506d0e7e897cc0dd02aaad510a5bdca</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DNA-BINDING TRANSCRIPTION FACTOR ACTIVITY, RNA POLYMERASE II-SPECIFIC&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to the ability of a protein to bind DNA and regulate the transcription of genes by RNA polymerase II."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7832e6342cbbf4e201eb3abbeccf544b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CHROMATIN BINDING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Chromatin binding refers to the interaction of proteins with chromatin, which is composed of DNA and histones, often playing a role in gene regulation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7832e6342cbbf4e201eb3abbeccf544b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARPC5L&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"ARPC5L is part of the Arp2/3 protein complex and plays roles in actin filament binding, nucleation, and cell migration."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3506d0e7e897cc0dd02aaad510a5bdca</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENTERIC NERVOUS SYSTEM DEVELOPMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Enteric nervous system development refers to the formation and maturation of the enteric nervous system, which regulates gastrointestinal function."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7832e6342cbbf4e201eb3abbeccf544b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARP2/3_PROTEIN_COMPLEX&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Arp2/3 protein complex is a group of proteins involved in actin nucleation and cytoskeletal organization."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Arp2/3 protein complex is involved in the regulation of actin filaments and cytoskeletal dynamics, playing a key role in processes like cell migration and adhesion."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3688619fce16d8bee5f1c0f6aea46a1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3506d0e7e897cc0dd02aaad510a5bdca</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OLFACTORY BULB DEVELOPMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Olfactory bulb development is the process by which the olfactory bulb, a part of the brain responsible for processing smell, forms during embryonic development."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7832e6342cbbf4e201eb3abbeccf544b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARF1 PATHWAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Arf1 pathway refers to signaling pathways involving ADP-ribosylation factor 1 (Arf1), which regulates vesicle transport and membrane trafficking in cells."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7832e6342cbbf4e201eb3abbeccf544b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EGF/EGFR SIGNALING PATHWAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The EGF/EGFR signaling pathway involves epidermal growth factor (EGF) binding to its receptor (EGFR), triggering cellular responses such as proliferation, differentiation, and survival."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7832e6342cbbf4e201eb3abbeccf544b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SIGNALING EVENTS MEDIATED BY FOCAL ADHESION KINASE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"This refers to signaling processes involving focal adhesion kinase (FAK), which plays a role in cell adhesion, migration, and survival."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7832e6342cbbf4e201eb3abbeccf544b</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ASNS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"ASNS is an enzyme active in the cytosol, playing a role in cellular processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"ASNS is involved in amino acid metabolism, particularly asparagine synthesis, and cellular responses to various stimuli like ER stress and nutrient levels."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d2e53da26ea23302e454287f8e030712&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc9205f03559e115e67a1fc1584e85bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ASPH&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"ASPH is involved in ion homeostasis and oxidative processes, functioning in the cytosol."&lt;SEP&gt;"ASPH is involved in multiple cellular functions such as ion homeostasis, stimuli-sensing channels, calcium ion binding, and various enzymatic activities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d2e53da26ea23302e454287f8e030712&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc9205f03559e115e67a1fc1584e85bd</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NEGATIVE_REGULATION_OF_APOPTOTIC_PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The suppression or inhibition of programmed cell death (apoptosis)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6af7852122b20fd32632d05ee60db0b3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ASPHD2&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"ASPHD2 enables dioxygenase activity, metal ion binding, and oxidoreductase activity, participating in cellular processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d2e53da26ea23302e454287f8e030712</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MASTL_FACILITATES_MITOTIC_PROGRESSION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"MASTL facilitates mitotic progression refers to the role of MASTL kinase in promoting events during the mitotic phase of the cell cycle."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3506d0e7e897cc0dd02aaad510a5bdca</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ASPM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"ASPM is involved in brain development, cell cycle regulation, and various developmental processes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d2e53da26ea23302e454287f8e030712</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PHOSPHATASE_INHIBITOR_ACTIVITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Phosphatase inhibitor activity involves molecules that inhibit phosphatases, enzymes responsible for removing phosphate groups from proteins."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3506d0e7e897cc0dd02aaad510a5bdca</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ASPSCR1&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"ASPSCR1 is involved in glucose homeostasis, protein transport, and regulation of cellular functions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d2e53da26ea23302e454287f8e030712</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOPAMINE_RECEPTOR_SIGNALING_PATHWAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The dopamine receptor signaling pathway involves the activation of dopamine receptors and downstream signaling processes in response to dopamine binding."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3506d0e7e897cc0dd02aaad510a5bdca</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SARCOPLASMIC RETICULUM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The sarcoplasmic reticulum is a type of smooth endoplasmic reticulum in muscle cells, involved in calcium ion storage and release; ASPH is located here."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d2e53da26ea23302e454287f8e030712</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CIRCADIAN_RHYTHM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Biological processes that follow a roughly 24-hour cycle, influenced by light and dark.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6af7852122b20fd32632d05ee60db0b3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PLASMA MEMBRANE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The plasma membrane is the boundary of a cell, separating its interior from the outside environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"The plasma membrane is the boundary of the cell, where ASPM and ASPSCR1 are located or interact with cellular components."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1e66c01e579691c0f359d019a8fc855d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2e53da26ea23302e454287f8e030712</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RNA_POLYMERASE_II_TRANSCRIPTION_REGULATOR_COMPLEX&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A complex involved in regulating transcription by RNA polymerase II, a key enzyme in gene expression."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6af7852122b20fd32632d05ee60db0b3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MITOTIC SPINDLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The mitotic spindle is a structure involved in cell division; ASPM plays a role in its organization and localization."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d2e53da26ea23302e454287f8e030712</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MEIOTIC SPINDLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The meiotic spindle is involved in the division of cells during meiosis; ASPM is involved in its assembly."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d2e53da26ea23302e454287f8e030712</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SEQUENCE-SPECIFIC_ DNA_BINDING.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The ability of proteins to bind specifically to certain DNA sequences, crucial for gene regulation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6af7852122b20fd32632d05ee60db0b3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;POSITIVE_REGULATION_OF_DNA_BIOSYNTHETIC_PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Positive regulation of DNA biosynthesis involves enhancing processes that synthesize DNA, essential for cell growth and replication."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-02805be411719fee5bfd259f3abcf8b6</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MICROTUBULE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Microtubules are cytoskeletal components involved in cell division and movement; ASPM interacts with them."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d2e53da26ea23302e454287f8e030712</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;POSITIVE_REGULATION_OF_GLUCONEOGENESIS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Positive regulation of gluconeogenesis involves processes that increase the production of glucose from non-carbohydrate precursors."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3506d0e7e897cc0dd02aaad510a5bdca</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MIDBODY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The midbody is a cellular structure involved in cytokinesis; ASPM is located here."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-d2e53da26ea23302e454287f8e030712</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CORTICOTROPIN-RELEASING_HORMONE.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Corticotropin-releasing hormone (CRH) signaling events involve the release and action of CRH, which regulates stress responses and the hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3506d0e7e897cc0dd02aaad510a5bdca</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ASTL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"ASTL enables several enzymatic activities including peptidase and metalloendopeptidase activity. It is involved in processes such as cell adhesion, fertilization, and proteolysis. ASTL is located in the cortical granule, cytoplasm, and plasma membrane."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6f08c5cd076b7b681114e08a434a3436</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAP2K_AND_MAPK_ACTIVATION.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"MAP2K and MAPK activation refers to the phosphorylation and activation of mitogen-activated protein kinases (MAPKs), which are involved in various cellular signaling pathways."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3506d0e7e897cc0dd02aaad510a5bdca</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ASTN1&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"ASTN1 is a protein involved in cell adhesion, migration, and neuronal functions. It is active in cellular components such as endosomes and clathrin-coated vesicles."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6f08c5cd076b7b681114e08a434a3436</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IL8-_AND_CXCR1-MEDIATED_SIGNALING_EVENTS.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"IL-8 and CXCR1-mediated signaling events involve the chemokine interleukin 8 (IL-8) binding to its receptor CXCR1, leading to cellular responses like chemotaxis."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3506d0e7e897cc0dd02aaad510a5bdca</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ASXL1&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"ASXL1 is a nuclear protein involved in various developmental processes including bone development, chromatin organization, and transcriptional regulation. It colocalizes with chromatin and has DNA binding abilities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6f08c5cd076b7b681114e08a434a3436</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CYTOPLASMIC_VESICLE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A cellular structure involved in transport within the cell."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6f08c5cd076b7b681114e08a434a3436</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAPK_SIGNALING_PATHWAY.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The MAPK signaling pathway is a series of molecular events that transmit signals from cell surface receptors to the nucleus, regulating processes like growth, differentiation, and apoptosis."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3506d0e7e897cc0dd02aaad510a5bdca</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CORTICAL_GRANULE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A granule found in the cortex of certain cells, particularly in oocytes, playing a role in processes like fertilization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Granules in the cortex of an oocyte that release enzymes during fertilization to prevent polyspermy."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6f08c5cd076b7b681114e08a434a3436</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HEDGEHOG_SIGNALING_EVENTS_MEDIATED_BY_GLI_PROTEINS.&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hedgehog signaling events mediated by Gli proteins refer to the downstream effects of Hedgehog ligand binding, particularly involving transcription factors like Gli that regulate target gene expression."</data>
